title: Opening Sequence — Path B: Rough Dock (No Brake)
story: no-signal-home
description: Tests docking without braking — good seal but tug drifts away on seal degradation

---

## Start in Tug Cargo Hold

> look
[OK: contains "Tug Cargo Hold"]
[OK: contains "alarm"]

## Move to cockpit and silence alarm

> south
[OK: contains "Tug Cockpit"]

> press button
[OK: contains "alarm"]
[OK: contains "Stillwater"]

## Examine docking controls (required before maneuver)

> examine docking controls
[OK: contains "MANEUVER"]

## Dock WITHOUT braking — skip brake step

> maneuver
[OK: contains_any "control" "thrusters" "manual"]

> extend arm
[OK: contains_any "clamp" "locked" "docking arm"]

## Check pressure (good seal path)

> check pressure
[OK: contains_any "pressure" "green" "seal"]

## Seal — should get good seal since pressure was checked

> seal
[OK: contains_any "Green" "green" "unlocks"]

## Board The Stillwater

> south
[OK: contains "Airlock"]
[STATE: true, yourself.location = Airlock]

## Wait 3 turns for seal degradation — tug should DRIFT AWAY (no brake)

> examine inspection window
[OK: contains_any "window" "docking"]

> examine claw marks
[OK: contains_any "claw" "gouges" "scratches"]

## Third turn after boarding — seal degrades, tug drifts away

> look
[OK: contains_any "shearing" "tumbling" "drifting" "sheared" "clamp"]
